On 12/31/2013 06:46 PM, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:
> Error in solve.default(B) :
>    system is computationally singular: reciprocal condition number =
> 1.12493e-16

I have found the problem, but I have not found (yet) a robust solution.
The problem is related to bivariate tables that contain lots of zeroes, eg

 > table(input$y.cdi5.t0,  input$y.cdi8.t0)

       0   1   2
   0 212  12   9
   1   2   0   0
   2   1   0   0

Usually, this is not problematic, but in this case, it clearly is.
Perhaps because there are several sparse bivariate tables, all involving
the same variable(s). Removing one of these variables (eg y.cdi5.t0)
seems to solve the problem.

Yves.

